      "side": 1,
      "message": "We already express the dependency in frameworks/base/Blueprints:\n\n    // framework.jar has a one-off dependency on the R.java and Manifest.java fi\nles\n    // generated by framework-res.apk\n    deps \u003d [\"framework-res\"],\n\nThe problem is expressing exactly what that dependency means - which generated files need to be pulled in, and to which compile step.  We could add something much more complicated, but it doesn\u0027t seem worth it for a one-off use.  If there are multiple other places that need to pull in R.java files then I can think about a solution that is more contained to Blueprints files, but if it is really one-off I prefer something like this, with appropriate comments.\n\nAs a counter-example of doing it in the build logic, look how much complexity is in frameworks/base/Android.mk to handle this dependency.  It has to know all about how the build system is building framework_res in order to extract the right files and dependencies.",
